ID: B3-Ch07a-Studied
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_magical_sense < 4)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_magical_sense >= 4)
#if(v_magical_sense < 4) {
 I turn my attention inward, straining to decipher the turbulence in the giant's aura. But tuning out the physical world for even a heartbeat is fatal against someone this fast. Gontrok closes the gap in an eyeblink, his fist shattering my skull before my senses can snap back to the room.

}
#if(v_magical_sense >= 4) {
 I narrow my magical sense, tracing the currents wrapping around the giant's frame. The anomaly jumps out instantly: the chaotic internal flow matches the precise signature of an active shapeshifter, but it lacks the balance of a full transformation. He is running a crude, modified variation of the spell to sprout wings and natural armor on command without changing his core anatomy. The shortcut leaves his aura fragile and deeply unstable. If I can hit the right focal points, that instability can be turned into a weapon.

A massive fist tears through the air where my head was a fraction of a second ago. I dive backward as Leila darts in from his blind side, keeping him off balance. Tactics race through my mind while dodging his relentless assault. Two approaches stand out, both adapting Reidzek's pressure-point technique to trigger a severe aura backlash.

If I can strike the key nodes at the base of his skull, the shock will induce violent vertigo and drop him to his knees. But getting inside his reach while he's targeting me is immensely dangerous. Alternatively, I could direct Leila to strike the pressure points while I draw his attention—though shouting complex anatomical adjustments over the roar of combat might prove impossible.

Either path carries lethal risk. It comes down to execution.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_magical_sense < 4)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_magical_sense < 4)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_magical_sense < 4)
choice("Perform the technique on Gontrok myself.", B3-Ch07a-Perform, v_current_scene = B3-Ch07a-Perform, v_b3_ch7_bet = 6) if (v_magical_sense >= 4)
choice("Tell Leila to perform the technique on Gontrok while I keep him busy.", B3-Ch07a-Busy, v_current_scene = B3-Ch07a-Busy, v_b3_ch7_bet = 7) if (v_magical_sense >= 4)


ID: B3-Ch07a-Perform
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_combat_technique < 2)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_combat_technique >= 2)
#if(v_b3_ch7_massage == 0) {
 I keep weaving around Gontrok's heavy swings until Leila cuts in from his left, forcing him to turn his shoulders. In that split second of distraction, I step into his blind spot, lock the fingertips of my right hand rigid, and drive three rapid strikes into the pressure nodes at the base of his neck. My magical sense tracks the impact, feeling for the disruption.

Improvising a technique I have never practiced proves tricky, but the strikes land true. The turbulent flow in his aura stutters and frays. Before I can complete the sequence, Gontrok whips his elbow around in a vicious backhand, forcing me to leap clear.

"What in the blazes was that?" Gontrok snarls, rubbing the back of his neck with a scowl. "A love tap? Take this fight seriously if you don't want your brains painted across the stone."

"Maybe land a hit before you start celebrating," I call back, catching my balance. "Your threats are sounding a little hollow."

}
#if(v_b3_ch7_massage == 1) {
 I keep weaving around Gontrok's heavy swings until Leila cuts in from his left, forcing him to turn his shoulders. In that split second of distraction, I step into his blind spot, lock the fingertips of my right hand rigid, and drive three rapid strikes into the pressure nodes at the base of his neck. My magical sense tracks the impact, feeling for the disruption.

Improvising a technique I failed to execute on Leila is clumsy work, but the strikes connect. The turbulent current in his aura wobbles. Before I can finish the chain, Gontrok throws a heavy elbow back toward my face, forcing me to dive away.

"What in the blazes was that?" Gontrok snarls, rubbing the back of his neck with a scowl. "A love tap? Take this fight seriously if you don't want your brains painted across the stone."

"Maybe land a hit before you start celebrating," I call back, catching my balance. "Your threats are sounding a little hollow."

}
#if(v_b3_ch7_massage == 2) {
 I keep weaving around Gontrok's heavy swings until Leila cuts in from his left, forcing him to turn his shoulders. In that split second of distraction, I step into his blind spot, lock the fingertips of my right hand rigid, and drive three rapid strikes into the pressure nodes at the base of his neck. Having practiced the flow on Leila earlier, my fingers find the precise channels instantly.

The unstable current in his aura immediately fractures, spiraling out of control. Before I can lock down the final node, Gontrok whips a massive elbow toward my temple, forcing me to spring backward.

"What in the blazes was that?" Gontrok snarls, rubbing the back of his neck with a scowl. "A love tap? Take this fight seriously if you don't want your brains painted across the stone."

"Maybe land a hit before you start celebrating," I call back, catching my balance. "Your threats are sounding a little hollow."

}
#if(v_combat_technique < 2) {
 "I'll hit you the moment you stop scurrying around like a headless rodent," Gontrok roars. "Stand and fight like a man instead of disgracing yourself with this cowardice!"

"I'll fight however I please, thanks," I say.

"Then take a coward's death," Gontrok spits.

He surges forward, unleashing a dizzying sequence of feints designed to bait my reflexes into dodging too early.

I predict the first two angles, but the rhythm shifts unpredictably. Relying entirely on raw reflex, I throw my weight into an evasive dive. Gontrok reads the stutter in my movement, adjusting mid-stride to deliver a crushing right hook that shatters my cranium in a single blow.

}
#if(v_combat_technique >= 2) {
 "I'll hit you the moment you stop scurrying around like a headless rodent," Gontrok roars. "Stand and fight like a man instead of disgracing yourself with this cowardice!"

"I'll fight however I please, thanks," I say.

"Then take a coward's death," Gontrok spits.

He surges forward, throwing a rapid sequence of feints meant to bait my reflexes into an early slip.

Thanks to my combat training, the pattern reveals itself after the first two swings. Whenever he throws a genuine strike, his back foot plants hard to drive weight into the blow; on the feints, his stance stays light and shallow. Reading the tells, I duck under the real punches and ignore the decoys, buying the vital seconds Leila needs to create our next opening.

}
