ID: B3-Ch07a-Busy
TEXT:

 I slip another heavy swing, waiting until Leila cuts across his flank. The moment Gontrok turns his shoulders, I shout instructions across the clash of steel.

"Leila! Use your father's temple technique on the back of his neck! Fingers locked together—strike the nerve nodes below the skull instead of using open palms!"

"How does that match my father's method?..." glowing blue letters flash in midair as Gontrok pauses, blinking in utter bewilderment.

"Same aura manipulation, different focal points!" I call out. "I'll call the targets!"

"A massage?" Gontrok rumbles, glaring at me like I've lost my mind. "Is this the raving of a condemned man? Come here and let me crush your throat."

"Leila, strike now!" I yell, lunging forward with my dagger to draw his guard.

"Steel won't bite, fool," Gontrok grunts, batting my blade aside.

Behind him, Leila drives her rigid fingers into his neck nodes, but her strikes lack the specific alignment needed to destabilize his current.

"And poking my neck won't save you either!" Gontrok snarls, throwing a blind elbow that forces her to leap clear.

"Again, lower on the left!" I shout, but the giant snaps back toward me, throwing a barrage of heavy punches that leaves no room for coaching.

Leila makes two more attempts while I scramble to survive, but translating subtle aura pressure points on the fly in the middle of a brawl proves impossible. As our momentum stalls, a familiar, relaxed presence steps out of the gloom and saunters into the corridor.

"Pardon the intrusion," Loyrang says in his customary lazy drawl, resting his palms near the twin hilts at his belt. "I was going to wait for the finish, but you're taking forever and I grew bored."

choice("Continue", B3-Ch07a-Loyrang, v_current_scene = B3-Ch07a-Loyrang)


ID: B3-Ch07a-Ignore
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_combat_technique < 2)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_combat_technique >= 2)
 

I decide against risking my neck on aura analysis and focus entirely on survival. Leila's distraction buys only a second before Gontrok pivots back, driving a heavy fist toward my chest. I leap clear, keeping my boots moving across the uneven stone.

Without weapons that can penetrate his hide, our only viable path is an attrition game—taking turns baiting his swings, dodging clean, and letting the giant exhaust himself. If we manage our stamina and trade off cleanly, his weight will eventually work against him.

After I slip three more violent hooks, Gontrok halts, eyeing me with sheer disdain from across the corridor.

"What is this strategy? Scurrying around until I die of old age?" Gontrok spits. "Take this fight seriously, or your next mistake will be your last."

"Maybe land a punch before delivering the lecture," I say, circling wide. "Your threats are losing their punch."

#if(v_combat_technique < 2) {
 "I'll hit you the moment you stop dancing like a coward," Gontrok growls. "Face me like a warrior!"

"I'll fight however I please, thanks," I answer.

"Then take a coward's grave," he snaps.

He lunges forward, unleashing an intricate sequence of feints to bait my reflexes into an early slip.

I predict the first two swings, but the rhythm shifts unpredictably. Relying purely on twitch reaction, I dive right. Gontrok reads the stutter in my motion, pivoting instantly to drive a crushing right hook through my skull.

}
#if(v_combat_technique >= 2) {
 "I'll hit you the moment you stop dancing like a coward," Gontrok growls. "Face me like a warrior!"

"I'll fight however I please, thanks," I answer.

"Then take a coward's grave," he snaps.

He lunges forward, throwing a rapid sequence of feints to bait an early dodge.

Thanks to my martial training, the mechanical tells are obvious. On a real strike, his back foot plants deep to transfer weight into the blow; on a feint, his weight stays balanced on his toes. Slipping the genuine punches and ignoring the decoys, I keep him frustrated until Leila darts in from his blind side, forcing him to leap backward to save his eyes.

}
