He explodes forward, his feints accelerating into a terrifyingly rapid flurry. The pace overwhelms my analytical read; under intense pressure, I misjudge an incoming shoulder dip and lean directly into the path of a devastating punch. The blow shatters my skull instantly, dropping me lifeless to the cavern floor.

}
#if(v_combat_technique >= 4) {
 "You're testing my patience," Gontrok rumbles, his gaze shifting between us.

He explodes forward, his feints accelerating into a blistering storm of strikes. But with my advanced martial mastery, the subtle tells in his stance remain entirely transparent regardless of speed. I duck and pivot around his reach, keeping him extended until Leila creates another opening from his flank.

We keep up the evasive rhythm for several minutes, but grinding down a giant's stamina is painfully slow work. Before we can wear him out, a familiar, nonchalant figure steps out of the gloom and strolls into the corridor.

"Pardon the interruption," Loyrang says in his customary relaxed drawl, hands resting casually near the hilts of his twin blades. "I was going to let you finish, but you're taking far too long and I grew bored."

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_combat_technique < 4)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_combat_technique < 4)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_combat_technique < 4)
choice("Continue", B3-Ch07a-Loyrang, v_current_scene = B3-Ch07a-Loyrang) if (v_combat_technique >= 4)


ID: B3-Ch07a-Weapons
TEXT:

 Seconds remain before Leila's sixty-second clock starts. How do we drop a giant without weapons that can pierce his hide? Think, Barry. Think.

"Whenever you're ready, princess," Gontrok says, squaring his stance. "The count starts the moment you make contact."

Leila nods once and drives her daggers toward his throat in a blinding flash. As before, the enchanted steel skitters off his tough hide with a dull metallic scrape, failing to break the skin.

"Is that your best?" Gontrok taunts, grinning down at her. "I expected something that might actually sting."

As Leila prepares another cut, the pieces click together in my head. A physical strike won't pierce his skin, but an aura shock doesn't need to break bone.

I step silently behind the giant, lock the fingers of my right hand rigid, and drive them in rapid succession into the nerve nodes at the base of his neck, feeling for the unstable current in his aura.

"Hey! Stop poking my neck, you little pest!" Gontrok barks, trying to shrug me off. "Have you lost your mind? Cut it out!"

"What's the matter, Gontrok?" Leila writes, stepping back into his field of view. "Afraid of a little massage?"

"I'm not afraid of anything!" Gontrok snarls. "He can poke all he wants. The second your minute runs out, I'm snapping his spine."

I tune out his shouting and keep my fingers working. If I can locate the primary junction of his shapeshifting current, the localized shock should induce severe vertigo and drop him to the floor. The moment his feet leave that spot, the wager is over.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch07a-Weapons2, v_current_scene = B3-Ch07a-Weapons2)


ID: B3-Ch07a-Weapons2
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch7_massage != 2) {
 Finding the right pressure points on a physiology this dense is proving harder than expected. Without a clean read on the flow, my strikes aren't generating enough force to disrupt the core current.

"Leila, I need help from the front," I call out. "Match my finger placement on his throat. I'm trying to trigger an aura backlash, but I can't find the central node."

"Why would you-- wait, I see the angle," Leila writes, tracking my hand movements. "Hold him steady."

She sheathes her daggers in a fluid motion, locks her fingers rigid, and presses firmly into the matching pressure points along his windpipe.

"You two are really beginning to get on my nerves, you know that?" Gontrok growls, his jaw tightening.

Leila ignores him completely, narrowing her focus. After two adjustments, her fingers settle on the primary nerve cluster. The moment she applies pressure, Gontrok's internal current fractures, cascading into wild, erratic convulsions.

"Ugh!" Gontrok groans, clutching his forehead with both hands as his knees buckle. "What did you do to me, you sneaky bastards?!"

"Well," I say, watching him take two clumsy steps backward to keep from collapsing. "It looks like you just lost the wager. You promised to stand on that exact stone for sixty seconds, and you just retreated two paces. You aren't going to deny that, are you?"

"I only stepped back because you cheated!" Gontrok roars through clenched teeth, shaking off the vertigo. "That wasn't an attack, it was some foul trick! It wasn't part of the deal!"

"And yet, you said very clearly earlier that you weren't going to cancel the bet because of what Barry was doing," Leila writes. "You also told me that I could attack your neck in whatever way I wanted, not only with my daggers. Are you saying that you are going back on your word?"

}
#if(v_b3_ch7_massage == 2) {
 Having dialed in the technique on Leila earlier, the tactile memory guides my hands instantly. My fingers find the key resonance points along his spine, driving a focused shockwave straight into his turbulent shapeshifting current. The giant's aura instantly fractures, collapsing into violent static.

"Ugh!" Gontrok grunts, clamping both hands to his skull as a massive wave of nausea hits him. "What did you do to me, you sneaky bastard?!"

"Just gave your aura a shove," I say, watching him stumble two full paces backward to keep from hitting the ground. "And more importantly, you broke your stance. You were supposed to stand on that mark for a full minute, and you just took two steps back. Going to deny it?"

"I only stepped back because you used a trick!" Gontrok snarls, his vision swimming. "That wasn't a real strike! It wasn't part of the wager!"

"And yet, you said very clearly earlier that you weren't going to cancel the bet because of what Barry was doing," Leila writes, stepping forward. "Are you saying that you are going back on your word?"

}
"No, of course not!" Gontrok spits, fighting through the dizziness. "A giant never breaks his oath!"

"So, you will let us go, then?" Leila writes, her expression serene.

"I-- my orders-- Argh! To the hells with it!" Gontrok growls, throwing his hands up in disgust. "You used cheap tricks, but a deal is a deal. I'd rather die than throw away my honor over two runts. Get out of my sight before I change my mind!"

"What did you just say?!" the illusionist's sharp voice cuts through the corridor.

The words bounce off every wall at once, carrying no physical source while his aura remains completely suppressed.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch07a-Loyrang, v_current_scene = B3-Ch07a-Loyrang)


ID: B3-Ch07a-Loyrang
TEXT:

achievement("An honorable victory",v_ac_b3_ch7_honorable)
#if(v_b3_ch7_bet == 1 || v_b3_ch7_bet == 2 || v_b3_ch7_bet == 6) {
 "Oh, is the entertainment finally over?" Loyrang's lazy drawl drifts from down the tunnel. His suppressed aura flares back to life as he strolls into view, hands resting casually near the hilts of his twin scimitars. "Thank the gods. I was about five seconds from falling asleep."

"What are you doing here, Loyrang?" the illusionist's disembodied voice demands. "You were ordered to assist with the assault on the rebel base."

"Pardon, what was your name again?" Loyrang asks, glancing toward a random shadow where he guesses the caster might be standing.

"My name is--" the illusionist starts.

"Doesn't matter," Loyrang cuts in smoothly. "I didn't come to talk to you. Hey, Gontrok, quick question. Do you know how to remove these collar devices below our throats? I've been trying to pry mine loose since yesterday, but it feels like it's grafted into the bone."

}
#if(v_b3_ch7_bet == 5 || v_b3_ch7_bet == 7) {
 "What are you doing here, Loyrang?" the illusionist's disembodied voice demands from the dark. "You were ordered to assist with the assault on the rebel base."

The royal guard's voice echoes off every stone surface, impossible to locate while his aura remains masked.

"Pardon, what was your name again?" Loyrang asks, glancing lazily toward the ceiling.

"My name is--" the illusionist begins.

"Doesn't matter," Loyrang interrupts. "I didn't come to talk to you anyway. Hey, Gontrok, quick question. Do you know how to remove these collar devices below our throats? I've been trying to pry mine loose since yesterday, but it feels like it's grafted into the bone."

}
#if(v_b3_ch7_bet == 1 || v_b3_ch7_bet == 2 || v_b3_ch7_bet == 5 || v_b3_ch7_bet == 6 || v_b3_ch7_bet == 7) {
 "Why would you want it off?" Gontrok asks, rubbing his temples. "Those collars are emergency recall beacons. The king uses them to summon us if he's in danger."

"Right, but purely hypothetically, if someone wanted to take one off, how would they go about it?" Loyrang asks.

"You can't remove it!" Gontrok rumbles. "They told us that the day we were sworn in. The only way that collar releases is if the king dies."

"I was afraid you'd say that..." Loyrang sighs.

"What is wrong with you, Loyrang?" Gontrok asks, his brow furrowing. "You're not making any sense."

"Isn't it obvious, you fool?" the illusionist's voice snaps. "He's deserting. He wants the king dead so he can flee the city without being recalled. Did you already forget he tried to slip away yesterday?"

"Watch your tongue," Gontrok growls. "That's my friend you're talking about."

"Actually, he's spot on," Loyrang says with a shrug. "Getting the king killed is exactly my plan."

"You're... you can't be serious," Gontrok stares at him in disbelief. "Why throw away everything we built here?"

}
choice(""If you want to kill the king, then you'd better wait in line! We were here first!"", B3-Ch07a-Line, v_current_scene = B3-Ch07a-Line)
choice(""What a coincidence! We want to kill the king too! Why don't we join forces?"", B3-Ch07a-Join, v_current_scene = B3-Ch07a-Join)
choice(""You're going to kill the king? Perfect! Less work for us, then!"", B3-Ch07a-Work, v_current_scene = B3-Ch07a-Work)


ID: B3-Ch07a-Line
TEXT:

 "If you want to kill the king, then you'd better wait in line! We were here first!"

"I can't lay a finger on him myself anyway," Loyrang says, waving a hand lazily. "The tournament geas still prevents me from harming local citizens, remember? My idea was to point you in the right direction so you can do the heavy lifting for me."

"Traitors, both of you!" the illusionist hisses from the shadows. "Gontrok, what are you waiting for? Cut him down!"

"Loyrang, why?" Gontrok pleads, looking torn. "We had a partnership! The king already promised to name me captain of the royal guard. All we have to do is convince him that the other cities are plotting against him, and we get full access to Ollendor's military arsenal. With the king as our puppet, we could conquer every kingdom on Varathia and rule the continent. Wasn't that the goal?"

"The king as your puppet?..." the illusionist echoes, sounding thoroughly flabbergasted. "Are you completely deaf to the fact that I am standing right here?!"

"Those were your grand ambitions, Gontrok, not mine," Loyrang replies, ignoring the invisible guard entirely. "I'm a mercenary. I fight for coin. Joining the royal guard seemed like easy gold at first, but lately the risk has outstripped the pay. Yesterday convinced me it's time to cut my losses and move on."

"So you were just going to vanish?" Gontrok shouts. "Without a word to me?"

"What was I supposed to say?" Loyrang asks. "Would you have walked away from your grand throne if I asked? Of course not. You're too deep in your own fantasy to listen to reason. Talking would have changed nothing."

"So you'd murder the king and burn all my plans to the ground?" Gontrok's voice shakes with fury.

"Think for ten seconds, Gontrok," Loyrang says, his tone hardening. "Your scheme was doomed from day one. You can't even have a private conversation without blabbing your coup to one of the king's most loyal subordinates. The king knew about your ambitions before you even finished unpacking. The only reason he kept you around was because he suspected the tournament organizers rigged the protection spell against Ollendor citizens, and he needed a heavy hitter to protect him from foreign participants. You're a disposable shield. The second the tournament concludes, he'll have you executed in your sleep."

"You don't know that!" Gontrok snarls.

"I know how rulers think," Loyrang counters calmly. "I saw his face every time you spoke to him. He doesn't trust you for a second. He's playing to your greed to keep you on a leash. That captaincy is a hollow title to keep you compliant until he's done with you. The moment your usefulness runs out, you're a dead man."

choice("Continue", B3-Ch07a-Vibrating, v_current_scene = B3-Ch07a-Vibrating)


ID: B3-Ch07a-Join
TEXT:

 "What a coincidence! We want to kill the king too! Why don't we join forces?"

"That was roughly my thought," Loyrang says with a casual grin. "I can't strike the final blow myself—the tournament protection spell prevents me from harming locals. But I can certainly provide you with blueprints, guard routes, and whatever else you need to finish the job."

"Traitors, the lot of you!" the illusionist's voice echoes in fury. "Gontrok, kill them now!"

"Loyrang, why?" Gontrok pleads, looking torn. "We had a partnership! The king already promised to name me captain of the royal guard. All we have to do is convince him that the other cities are plotting against him, and we get full access to Ollendor's military arsenal. With the king as our puppet, we could conquer every kingdom on Varathia and rule the continent. Wasn't that the goal?"

"The king as your puppet?..." the illusionist echoes, sounding thoroughly flabbergasted. "Are you completely deaf to the fact that I am standing right here?!"

"Those were your grand ambitions, Gontrok, not mine," Loyrang replies, ignoring the invisible guard entirely. "I'm a mercenary. I fight for coin. Joining the royal guard seemed like easy gold at first, but lately the risk has outstripped the pay. Yesterday convinced me it's time to cut my losses and move on."

"So you were just going to vanish?" Gontrok shouts. "Without a word to me?"

"What was I supposed to say?" Loyrang asks. "Would you have walked away from your grand throne if I asked? Of course not. You're too deep in your own fantasy to listen to reason. Talking would have changed nothing."

"So you'd murder the king and burn all my plans to the ground?" Gontrok's voice shakes with fury.

"Think for ten seconds, Gontrok," Loyrang says, his tone hardening. "Your scheme was doomed from day one. You can't even have a private conversation without blabbing your coup to one of the king's most loyal subordinates. The king knew about your ambitions before you even finished unpacking. The only reason he kept you around was because he suspected the tournament organizers rigged the protection spell against Ollendor citizens, and he needed a heavy hitter to protect him from foreign participants. You're a disposable shield. The second the tournament concludes, he'll have you executed in your sleep."

"You don't know that!" Gontrok snarls.

"I know how rulers think," Loyrang counters calmly. "I saw his face every time you spoke to him. He doesn't trust you for a second. He's playing to your greed to keep you on a leash. That's why he made you captain. He knows what you want and feeds it to you to keep you tame. But the moment your usefulness runs out, you're getting put down."

choice("Continue", B3-Ch07a-Vibrating, v_current_scene = B3-Ch07a-Vibrating)


ID: B3-Ch07a-Work
TEXT:

 "You're going to kill the king? Perfect! Less work for us, then!"

"Don't get ahead of yourself," Loyrang says with a chuckle. "When I said I'd get him killed, I meant I would set up the kill for you. The tournament spell prevents me from harming locals, remember? You'll still have to do the actual swinging."

"Traitors, the lot of you!" the illusionist's voice echoes in fury. "Gontrok, kill them now!"

"Loyrang, why?" Gontrok pleads, looking torn. "We had a partnership! The king already promised to name me captain of the royal guard. All we have to do is convince him that the other cities are plotting against him, and we get full access to Ollendor's military arsenal. With the king as our puppet, we could conquer every kingdom on Varathia and rule the continent. Wasn't that the goal?"

